    <http://example.org/node/chunk1> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Public Tender - Centre Hospitalier Régional de Belval (CHRB) Implementation of an AI assistance solution for hospital staff 1." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message0> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk10> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "The solution must let staff quickly access reliable, up-to-date information drawn from the authority's internal procedures, care protocols and HAS recommendations, applicable regulatory texts, and internal documents (guides, notes, reference frameworks, drug references)." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message0> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk100> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Support for health interoperability standards (HL7 / FHIR), national health identifier (INS), and national framework (Ségur du numérique en santé, Mon espace santé / DMP) is FULLY COVERED with production-ready FHIR HL7 connector, INS support, and framework alignment." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message3> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk101> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Hosting on SecNumCloud-qualified infrastructure or equivalent is FULLY COVERED through the Sovereign HDS tier provided by OuraneCloud, which is SecNumCloud-qualified and HDS-certified. the proposed architecture would be based on our Atelier platform, utilizing the Sovereign European open-weight model hosted by Faber IA on OuraneCloud Sovereign HDS tier, with integration to the client's SIH and DPI systems through standard connectors or custom adapters as necessary. our Atelier platform will operate 24/7, meeting the required availability target, and provide response times below 2 seconds for common queries." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message3> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk102> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "The client's global budget is 900,000 over 5 years." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message5> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk103> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Annual operating costs must remain controlled and compatible with the authority's budgetary capacity." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message5> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk104> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "The tender requires a pilot phase followed by progressive rollout." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message5> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk105> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Given our pricing model and current financial position, what is our projected margin on The tender, and are there cost-optimisation strategies our can propose?" ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message5> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk106> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Based on our pricing model, the target gross margin percentage ranges from 25% to 35%." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message5> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk107> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Given the reference budget of €900,000 over 5 years, our financial capacity note indicates that our meet the typical thresholds for The tender." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message5> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk108> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "To project our projected margin on this contractur need to consider the cost structure, including one-off project costs and recurring run costs. one-off project costs are estimated to be around 30% of the reference budget of €900,000 over 5 years, which is €270,000, spread over 18 months. recurring run costs would account for approximately 70% of the reference budget of €900,000 over 5 years, which is €630,000, over 5 years. our main recurring cost drivers are hosting and inference costs, which can vary depending on the chosen tier and model." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message5> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk109> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "To optimize costs, our could propose the sovereign HDS tier and the sovereign European model, as the sovereign HDS tier and the sovereign European model are more cost-efficient on the recurring side compared to the premium high-availability tier combined with top-tier proprietary inference." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message5> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk11> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "The solution must contextualise The solution answers to the staff member's request. 3.2 Drafting assistance." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message0> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk110> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "By choosing a more cost-efficient configuration, our can potentially increase our projected margin on this contract while keeping the annual operating costs controlled and compatible with the authority's budgetary capacity. our finance role will work closely with the architect to ensure that a more cost-efficient configuration stays within the authority's budget envelope and preserves an acceptable margin." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message5> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk111> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "The tender requires strict GDPR compliance (EU-only data hosting, no transfer outside EU, encryption and pseudonymisation of sensitive data where applicable), French Hébergeur de Données de Santé (HDS) certification for the infrastructure hosting the solution, and explainability and traceability of recommendations or suggestions produced by the solution." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message7> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk112> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "What security risks should we flag, and are we compliant with these requirements? we are compliant with the EU-only data hosting requirement as we hosting partner is OuraneCloud, a SecNumCloud-qualified sovereign cloud. we also comply with the no transfer outside EU requirement since we infrastructure is operated on OuraneCloud, a SecNumCloud-qualified sovereign cloud.  we solution implements encryption in transit using TLS 1.3 and encryption at rest using AES-256, which fulfills the EU-only data hosting requirement." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message7> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk113> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Additionally, we support pseudonymisation of sensitive data where applicable." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message7> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk114> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Regarding HDS certification, we hosting infrastructure operated on OuraneCloud, a SecNumCloud-qualified sovereign cloud holds HDS certification, ensuring compliance with French health-data hosting regulations.  the solutionorts explainability and traceability of recommendations or suggestions produced by the solution, which aligns with the requirements for explainability and traceability." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message7> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk115> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "As for security risks to flag, we should ensure that we defined remediation SLAs by severity for vulnerability management are strictly followed to minimize potential vulnerabilities." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message7> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk116> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Moreover, it is crucial that we incident response plan, including detection, notification, and remediation steps, is effectively executed in case of a breach, adhering to the 72-hour breach notification delay." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message7> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk117> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Overall, based on the provided context, we appear to be compliant with the specified requirements, but ongoing vigilance regarding vulnerability management and incident response is necessary to mitigate potential security risks." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message7> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk118> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "The tender requires that no clinical or medico-administrative decision may be automated without explicit validation by a qualified professional, and that the solution must not require medical-device qualification (CE marking / MDR)." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message9> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk119> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "What legal risks should we flag, and are we compliant with these regulatory requirements? we should flag potential legal risks related to medical device qualification and liability. we use of AI models in a health context may approach the medical-device threshold, and it is crucial to ensure that we solution does not require CE marking or MDR qualification.  we Legal function is responsible for monitoring regulatory obligations, including the EU AI Act requirements for AI systems used in a health context, and flagging potential CE/MDR implications. we are compliant with the requirement that no clinical or medico-administrative decision may be automated without explicit validation by a qualified professional, as our solution IP model is based on proprietary software licensed to the client under a subscription/usage model, which allows for human oversight and validation." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message9> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk12> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "The solution must assist the drafting of clinical and administrative content, notably discharge summaries and medical reports (comptes-rendus), medical correspondence and patient letters, administrative documents and dossier syntheses." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message0> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk120> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Regarding the medical-device threshold, Our Legal function monitors obligations related to health deployment, including HDS framework and Medical confidentiality. we have a process in place to flag potential CE/MDR implications and assess the consequences for liability and positioning when a use case approaches the medical-device threshold." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message9> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk121> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Therefore, we can ensure that our solution is designed to avoid requiring medical-device qualification, and we are compliant with the requirement that no clinical or medico-administrative decision may be automated without explicit validation by a qualified professional." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message9> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk122> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "The client requires an intelligent assistance tool capable of supporting hospital staff in hospital staff clinical-administrative activities, including retrieval of information from internal procedures, care protocols and applicable regulation, assistance in drafting medical and administrative documents, support in handling dossiers, and support for the continuity of care between professionals." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message11> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk123> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "What AI components and innovation strategy can we propose to meet these requirements? we can propose an AI-powered assistant that leverages we retrieval-augmented generation capabilities, grounded in the hospital's own validated documents, to support clinical-administrative activities." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message11> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk124> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "The core approach will utilize hybrid retrieval, re-ranking, query reformulation, and multi-document synthesis to provide relevant information and drafting assistance." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message11> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk125> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "The assistant can be designed to provide template-guided drafting for medical and administrative documents, such as discharge summaries and medical correspondence, as well as structured extraction to assist with tasks like PMSI/ICD-10 coding." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message11> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk126> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Additionally, The assistant can recall applicable rules and regulations during dossier handling and suggest next steps based on the dossier context." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message11> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk127> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "To ensure continuity of care, The assistant can generate structured handover summaries, allowing professionals to efficiently take over in-progress dossiers with full context. we iterative approach will involve corpus selection and curation with the hospital's experts, retrieval tuning, prompt and template design per use case, and an evaluation loop to measure answer quality." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message11> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk128> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "In terms of innovation strategy, we can embed The assistant into the hospital staff's existing work environment and tools, avoiding disruption to clinical or administrative workflows." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message11> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk129> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "The assistant will be designed to augment existing practices, with staff interacting through staff current interfaces. designed has demonstrated efficiency outcomes in comparable deployments, reducing processing and documentation times by surfacing information and drafting content at the point of need. we prior experience with a medical-documentation pilot for a regional hospital group can serve as a relevant reference point for this project, providing valuable insights into the development and deployment of such an assistant." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message11> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk13> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Generated content must be adapted to the clinical/administrative context and conform to expected quality standards. 3.3 Dossier-handling assistance." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message0> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk130> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "The client wishes to limit the environmental footprint of The client information systems and proposes a solution that contributes to reducing energy consumption and relies on low-carbon infrastructure." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message13> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk131> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "What sustainability strategies can we propose to reduce the environmental impact of we solution? we can propose several sustainability strategies to reduce the environmental impact of our solution, including model right-sizing, caching, and batching, which are part of we digital sobriety practices." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message13> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk132> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Additionally, we can highlight we partnership with green hosting partners like OuraneCloud, which uses renewable energy and has a power usage effectiveness of 1.2, as well as heat reuse capabilities. we also conduct bilan carbone and have a published trajectory to reduce carbon intensity per managed assistant year on year, which demonstrates we commitment to reducing we environmental footprint." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message13> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk133> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Furthermore, we can offer to report the deployment footprint to the client, providing transparency on the environmental impact of our solution." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message13> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk134> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "The Centre Hospitalier Régional de Belval (CHRB) can rely on our consortium to design, implement, and deploy an artificial intelligence solution that assists hospital staff in hospital staff daily activities. our proposed solution, based on the Atelier platform, utilizes the Sovereign European open-weight model hosted by Faber IA on OuraneCloud's Sovereign HDS tier, ensuring compliance with regulatory requirements such as GDPR, HDS certification, and medical confidentiality. the Atelier platform provides an intelligent assistance tool, accessible from hospital staff's work environment, supporting clinical-administrative activities including retrieval of information from internal procedures, care protocols, and applicable regulations. an artificial intelligence solution that assists hospital staff in their daily activities assists in drafting medical and administrative documents, handling dossiers, and facilitating continuity of care between professionals and services. our leverage hybrid retrieval, re-ranking, query reformulation, and multi-document synthesis to provide relevant information and drafting assistance." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message14> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk135> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "The proposed architecture integrates with the existing hospital information system (SIH) and electronic patient record (DPI) through standard connectors or custom adapters as necessary, supporting health interoperability standards such as HL7/FHIR, national health identifier (INS), and national framework (Ségur du numérique en santé, Mon espace santé/DMP). our operation is 24/7, meeting the required availability target of 99.9%, and providing response times below 2 seconds for common queries." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message14> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk136> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "To optimize costs, our propose a cost-efficient configuration utilizing OuraneCloud's Sovereign HDS tier and the Sovereign European open-weight model hosted by Faber IA on OuraneCloud's Sovereign HDS tier, which reduces hosting and inference costs." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message14> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk137> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "The one-off project costs are estimated at €270,000, spread over 18 months, while recurring run costs account for approximately €630,000 over 5 years. our finance role will work closely with the architect to ensure that a cost-efficient configuration utilizing the sovereign HDS tier and the sovereign European model, which reduces hosting and inference costs stays within the authority's budget envelope and preserves an acceptable margin. an artificial intelligence solution that assists hospital staff in their daily activities implements encryption in transit using TLS 1.3 and encryption at rest using AES-256, fulfilling the encryption requirement." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message14> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk138> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Additionally, our support pseudonymisation of sensitive data where applicable." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message14> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk139> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Our proposed solution, based on the Atelier platform supports explainability and traceability of recommendations or suggestions produced by an artificial intelligence solution that assists hospital staff in their daily activities, aligning with the requirements for explainability and traceability. our are compliant with the EU-only data hosting requirement as our hosting partner is OuraneCloud's. our infrastructure is operated on OuraneCloud's, ensuring compliance with the no transfer outside EU-only requirement. our also comply with HDS certification, as Our infrastructure holds HDS certification." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message14> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk14> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "The solution must assist staff in analysing and handling dossiers by surfacing relevant information, recalling applicable rules, and suggesting actions or verifications." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message0> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk140> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "To mitigate potential security risks, our will ensure that our defined remediation SLAs by severity for vulnerability management are strictly followed and that our incident response plan is effectively executed in case of a breach, adhering to the 72-hour breach notification delay. our Legal function monitors regulatory obligations, including EU AI Act requirements for AI systems used in a health context, and flags potential CE/MDR implications. an artificial intelligence solution that assists hospital staff in their daily activities is designed as an assistance tool, ensuring that no clinical or medico-administrative decision is automated without explicit validation by a qualified professional. our have a process in place to flag potential CE/MDR implications and assess the consequences for liability and positioning when a use case approaches the medical-device threshold." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message14> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk141> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "To reduce the environmental impact of an artificial intelligence solution that assists hospital staff in their daily activities, our propose several sustainability strategies, including model right-sizing, caching, and batching, as part of our digital sobriety practices. our highlight our partnership with green hosting partners like OuraneCloud's, which uses renewable energy and has a power usage effectiveness of 1.2, as well as heat reuse capabilities. our conduct bilan carbone and have a published trajectory to reduce carbon intensity per managed assistant year on year, demonstrating our commitment to reducing our environmental footprint." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message14> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk142> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "The project will be conducted progressively, with a pilot phase on a limited perimeter (one or two departments) followed by progressive generalisation to all services." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message14> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk143> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Change-management support and staff training are expected, ensuring that an artificial intelligence solution that assists hospital staff in their daily activities is embedded into the hospital staff's existing work environment and tools, avoiding disruption to clinical or administrative workflows. our prior experience with a medical-documentation pilot for a regional hospital group serves as a relevant reference point for The project, providing valuable insights into the development and deployment of such an assistant. our are confident that an artificial intelligence solution that assists hospital staff in their daily activities meets the requirements outlined in the call for tenders, providing a high-quality artificial intelligence assistance tool that improves the efficiency of hospital staff and the quality and safety of care delivered to patients, while ensuring compliance with regulatory requirements and reducing environmental impact." ;
